WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.266 --> 00:00:02.335 align:start size:94% position:6%
-So your father was
in the theater as well.

00:00:02.335 --> 00:00:03.803 align:start size:94% position:6%
He was an actor,
director, producer.

00:00:03.803 --> 00:00:06.840 align:start size:94% position:6%
And he directed
you and your siblings, yes?

00:00:06.840 --> 00:00:08.908 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yes.
-What was that like?

00:00:08.908 --> 00:00:10.410 line:92%
How was he as a director?

00:00:10.410 --> 00:00:11.378 line:92%
-Well, he was high energy.

00:00:11.378 --> 00:00:15.315
He used to use a kitchen timer
to make sure that the actors

00:00:15.315 --> 00:00:18.084 align:start size:94% position:6%
got the scene over
before it went off.

00:00:18.084 --> 00:00:20.086 line:92%
Now, that was kind of his style.

00:00:20.086 --> 00:00:21.755 line:92%
-Not a lot of long pauses.

00:00:21.755 --> 00:00:22.455 size:78% position:39% line:92%
-The man was amazing.

00:00:22.455 --> 00:00:27.260 align:start size:94% position:6%
He produced and -- He produced
all of Shakespeare's plays

00:00:27.260 --> 00:00:31.398
and directed many of them,
and we were a theater family.

00:00:31.398 --> 00:00:35.101 align:start size:94% position:6%
I was on stage at age 2.
-Oh, my goodness.

00:00:35.101 --> 00:00:39.572
-Playing one of Nora's children
in "Doll's House."

00:00:39.572 --> 00:00:42.308 align:start size:94% position:6%
I don't remember
anything about it,

00:00:42.308 --> 00:00:45.612 align:start size:94% position:6%
but I'm told I was very good.
-Yeah, yeah.

00:00:45.612 --> 00:00:47.781 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:00:47.781 --> 00:00:50.884
-No, it was a big deal
when I finally had lines.

00:00:50.884 --> 00:00:52.118 size:78% position:39% line:92%
-Oh, yeah, I imagine.

00:00:52.118 --> 00:00:52.852 line:92%
-I was about 7 years old.

00:00:52.852 --> 00:00:56.856 align:start size:94% position:6%
-And then you had the chance
to direct your father.

00:00:56.856 --> 00:00:57.290 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Yeah.

00:00:57.290 --> 00:00:59.325 align:start size:94% position:6%
-And what was he like
as an actor?

00:00:59.325 --> 00:01:00.794 line:92%
Did he take direction well?

00:01:00.794 --> 00:01:03.163 align:start size:94% position:6%
-He was, I would say, fustian.
-Okay.

00:01:03.163 --> 00:01:07.567 align:start size:94% position:6%
-He was like an old-time
Shakespeare actor.

00:01:07.567 --> 00:01:11.604 align:start size:94% position:6%
I sort of had to calm him down
a little bit.

00:01:11.604 --> 00:01:12.505 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:01:12.505 --> 00:01:13.440 size:78% position:39% line:92%
But he was fantastic.

00:01:13.440 --> 00:01:17.510
You know, his -- Shakespeare
productions, when I was a kid,

00:01:17.510 --> 00:01:21.614
were done on a unit stage
outdoors in the summertime

00:01:21.614 --> 00:01:24.350 align:start size:94% position:6%
with huge crowds
and no amplification.

00:01:24.350 --> 00:01:24.784 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Oh, wow.

00:01:24.784 --> 00:01:28.088
-So I figured he was -- he was
entitled to that grand style.

00:01:28.088 --> 00:01:28.588 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Of course.

00:01:28.588 --> 00:01:30.723 align:start size:94% position:6%
And the audience was probably
very happy

00:01:30.723 --> 00:01:32.025 line:92%
that he entitled them with it.

00:01:32.025 --> 00:01:33.993 size:75% position:38%
-Yeah. They could --
They could hear him.

00:01:33.993 --> 00:01:37.730
-You did the show. You've been
doing it for about 10 years.

00:01:37.730 --> 00:01:38.832 line:92%
You've taken it on the road.

00:01:38.832 --> 00:01:42.202
And was it North Carolina
where you had a moment --

00:01:42.202 --> 00:01:44.938
another moment where you had
to interact with the audience?

00:01:44.938 --> 00:01:46.439 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Where did you find out
about all these?

00:01:46.439 --> 00:01:48.641 align:start size:94% position:6%
-We do -- We do our digging.
We do our digging.

00:01:48.641 --> 00:01:50.310 align:start size:94% position:6%
-No, I -- again,
"Stories by Heart"

00:01:50.310 --> 00:01:51.411 line:92%
in Greensboro, North Carolina,

00:01:51.411 --> 00:01:54.647
I came out and talked to the
audience, chatted with them

00:01:54.647 --> 00:01:58.118
for about five minutes then
finally sat down to begin

00:01:58.118 --> 00:02:00.954 line:92%
the sort of body of the work,

00:02:00.954 --> 00:02:04.157 align:start size:94% position:6%
and I looked down,
and my fly was open.

00:02:04.157 --> 00:02:04.657 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:02:04.657 --> 00:02:08.394 align:start size:94% position:6%
And there, again, I had two
hours to go,

00:02:08.394 --> 00:02:09.863 line:92%
and I looked at the crowd,

00:02:09.863 --> 00:02:12.132 align:start size:94% position:6%
and I stood up and said,
"I'm so sorry.

00:02:12.132 --> 00:02:16.269
Did anybody notice that my fly
has been open all this time?"

00:02:16.269 --> 00:02:19.506 size:75% position:38%
And a couple of them
raised their hand.

00:02:19.506 --> 00:02:20.039 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:02:20.039 --> 00:02:24.577 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I said,
"Why didn't you tell me?

00:02:24.577 --> 00:02:26.913 size:78% position:39% line:92%
I am so embarrassed."

00:02:26.913 --> 00:02:27.547 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
They loved it.

00:02:27.547 --> 00:02:29.849 align:start size:94% position:6%
It was the best
the show ever went.

00:02:29.849 --> 00:02:33.520
In fact, there were people who
thought it was part of the show.

00:02:33.520 --> 00:02:34.053 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:02:34.053 --> 00:02:35.722 align:start size:94% position:6%
-You have too much integrity
for that.

00:02:35.722 --> 00:02:36.956 line:92%
You would never fake a fly down.

00:02:36.956 --> 00:02:38.525 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Actually,
I've thought about it.

00:02:38.525 --> 00:02:40.894 align:start size:94% position:6%
-It's always so great
to see you.

